{{if not .Global.Config.Published}}
> [!TIP]
> To finish publishing your SDK you must [run your first generation action](https://www.speakeasy.com/docs/github-setup#step-by-step-guide).
{{end}}

The SDK relies on [Composer](https://getcomposer.org/) to manage its dependencies.

{{- if .Global.Config.Published}}

To install the SDK and add it as a dependency to an existing `composer.json` file:
```bash
composer require "{{.Global.Config.PackageName}}"
```
{{- else}}

To install the SDK first add the below to your `composer.json` file:

```json
{
    "repositories": [
        {
            "type": "github",
            "url": "{{default "<UNSET>" .Global.Config.InstallationURL}}{{if not (hasSuffix ".git" .Global.Config.InstallationURL)}}.git{{end}}"
        }
    ],
    "require": {
        "{{.Global.Config.PackageName}}": "*"
    }
}
```

Then run the following command:

```bash
composer update
```
{{- end}}